Recorded narration clips live here, one per cueId.

Filename = the cueId with every character outside [A-Za-z0-9._-] replaced by
an underscore, plus an audio extension. `parade:counting-prompt-r0` becomes
`parade_counting-prompt-r0.wav`. See narrationClipStem() in
app/lib/platform/narration_audio.dart and the identical transform in
tools/tts/record/index.html.

Nothing here is required. NarrationPlayer plays a clip when it finds one and
speaks the line through system TTS when it doesn't, so clips can land one at a
time. Drop files in, rebuild, and those lines are in a human voice.

WAV is the safe format: Chrome, Safari and iOS all decode it, which webm/opus
does not manage. This folder is NOT touched by scripts/sync-assets.sh.
